couple of weekends ago me and the boys  at a game Jam called ladum dare or  ludume we had 72 hours to make a game  based on the theme every 10 seconds this  time around we made something that we  were actually really happy with a puzzle  game called dichotomy a word that none  of us had ever heard of before in every  dichotomy level your goal is to reach  the flag you have 10 seconds to execute  any kind of maneuver you want in the  sandbox before your moves are played out  in what we call the real world the  actual level being the real world though  it's full of danger with various deadly  tiles and traps that make completing a  level more and more difficult as you  progress through the game but we weren't  completely heartless we just had to give  you guys a Fighting Chance of completing  our game you have two abilities well  three I guess if you can count Movement  we brilliantly consider not adding move  into the game to make it a bit more  challenging but the undecided against it  anyway two abilities firstly tile reveal  space bar sandbox shows you the tiles  that would be immediately around you in  the real world now the best aspect of  this feature is the ultimate despair it  gives you when user's ability and  realize that actually you are already  already dead but you have to wait for  your time to finish in the sandbox  before you can dive for real inevitably  the player learns that the game is not  so much dichotomy as it is  dichotomy the second ability we've given  the player is the ability to slow down  time and that is really useful because  you can watch your shattered lifeless  player fall to bits in slow motion as  the field of view of the camera goes oh  I guess sometimes it will help you dodge  those swinging killing things when  playing dichotomy it's better not to  think of dichotomy as just a game or  some kind of puzzle to solve think of it  more as a simulation of your life in the  beginning the first 11 levels are so New  Jersey you go through the game facing a  series of mild challenges  some might seem difficult at the time  but you are able to overcome them think  of this as your childhood where your  parents cared and provided for you and  most of your difficulties were  self-inflicted only after completing the  first 11 levels will you begin to  experience the five stages of playing  dichotomy stage one denial you tell  yourself that you don't need to complete  this next level  stage two anger you break your monitor  keyboard and rage at the game and people  around you become seriously alarmed  stage three sadness you become all sad  and miserable because you can't beat a  level in a game made by Studio channel  for a game Jam stage 4 acceptance you  accept the fact that you won't be able  to beat this level and you delete it  Stage 5 reinvention you create your own  level and beat it oh what's this you  didn't know that we had a morning  support into this game out of the world  from the game every dichotomy map is an  11 by 11 pixel PNG image file stored in  this levels directory the game  automatically loads and plays levels in  alphabetical order from this directory  inside the image file every pixel  represents a tile there are three layers  in our levels which map to the red green  and blue values of each pixel with each  layer storing information about what is  contained within that tile by utilizing  different channels of the image we're  able to store more information about  exactly what should be at that tile in  the game let's take a look at this level  as an example if we look at the color of  this pixel we'll see that it has a red  value of 150 and a green value of 150  which means that the base tile is an  ocean deadly tile and there's a bridge  on top of it and that's how levels work  in dichotomy you can play our game for  free by going to the link below let us  know what you think and thanks for  watching
 

